  "description_detailed": "To celebrate the 25th anniversary of the cinema release of the first chapter of Peter Jackson's trilogy, Monnaie de Paris will unveil a collection of precious coins dedicated to the legendary Lord of the Rings series in 2026. From the Shire to Mordor, the perilous journey of the Fellowship of the Ring is now engraved in metal, celebrating a mythical saga that has become a true pillar of the fantasy genre.A creature broken by time and by the one Ring, Gollum lives on the margins of society, torn between what he once was and what he has become. Once a Hobbit, he now bears the marks of an obsession that has slowly consumed him, erasing almost all traces of innocence.Both guide and threat, victim and servant of the Ring, he embodies the fragility of beings faced with the corrupting power of Mordor. His journey reminds us that the deepest shadows often arise from misguided attachment, and that no one is entirely lost as long as a glimmer of light remains.",
